  "problem": "Given $Z=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,$ what is $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Z))?$",
  "worked_solution": "To find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Z))$, we reduce $Z$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Z & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{5} & :={R}_{5}+(-\\frac{2}{3}){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $4$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $4$th column). \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Z))=1.\n$$",
